# --- CryptoHack: private working notebook, never published ---
# Their FAQ asks that solutions and writeups not be published outside the
# platform (exception: Starter challenges and those worth <= 25 points), and
# these files embed CryptoHack's own challenge descriptions verbatim.
# site/scripts/sync.mjs reads them locally and emits only what policy allows.
writeups/cryptohack/
cryptohack_catalog.json

# --- Challenge Lab answers ---
# The challenges themselves are committed — that's the work worth showing. The
# answers are not: stripping author notes from the published page is pointless
# if the source file naming the key sits in a public repo.
challenges/flags.json
challenges/notes/

# --- Node deps anywhere (challenge instances install their own) ---
node_modules/

# --- Astro site ---
site/node_modules/
site/dist/
site/.astro/

# Local-only scaffolding — kept on disk, never published
TEMPLATE.md

# --- Gated training content ---
# Lesson PLAINTEXT and the access code never go in the repo. Only the encrypted
# output (site/src/data/lessons.json) is committed, so the repo leaks no Q&A.
# training/encrypt.mjs runs locally, like sync.mjs.
training/lessons/
training/access-code.txt

# Scratch space for solving, not part of the published site
practice-files-for-ctfs/

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/
